  "worked_solution": "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe increment in $y$ using the Runge-Kutta (RK4) method with step size $\u0394x$ is computed as the weighted average of four sample slopes:\n\n$$\n\u0394y=\\frac{1}{6}({y}^{\u2032}+2{y}_{1}^{\u2032}+2{y}_{2}^{\u2032}+{y}_{3}^{\u2032})\\cdot \u0394x,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}^{\u2032}=f(x,y)$ is the estimated slope at the point $(x,y),$\n\n- ${y}_{1}^{\u2032}=f({x}_{1},{y}_{1})$ is the estimated slope at $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(x+\\frac{1}{2}\u0394x,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{\u2032}\\cdot \u0394x),$\n\n- ${y}_{2}^{\u2032}=f({x}_{2},{y}_{2})$ is the estimated slope at $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(x+\\frac{1}{2}\u0394x,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{1}^{\u2032}\\cdot \u0394x),$\n\n- ${y}_{3}^{\u2032}=f({x}_{3},{y}_{3})$ is the estimated slope at $({x}_{3},{y}_{3})=(x+\u0394x,\\,y+{y}_{2}^{\u2032}\\cdot \u0394x).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
